    },
    {
      "at": 1.5,
      "text": "At the apex the red vertical arrow shrinks to nothing, while the blue horizontal arrow keeps its length."
    },
    {
      "at": 2.4,
      "text": "On the way down the red arrow points downward and grows again: gravity acts vertically, never horizontally."
    },
    {
      "at": 3.2,
      "text": "The path is a parabola because x grows linearly while y is quadratic in t."
    }
  ],
  "fallback": {
    "text": "Static trajectory plot: with v0 = 20 m/s at 55°, vx0 = 11.5 m/s and vy0 = 16.4 m/s, so x = 11.5t and y = 16.4t − 4.9t². Marks at t = 0, 1, 2, 3.3 s show constant horizontal steps, decreasing then increasing vertical steps, vy = 0 at t = 1.67 s while vx stays 11.5 m/s, and landing at about 38 m."
  },
